  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 242 AM Monday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... A typical cool to mild and dry stretch of October \nweather for NC this week. \n\nLow pressure will remain over the western Atlantic as it wobbles \naround the next few days. In turn, strong surface high pressure \nareas will move from the Midwest to New England this week that will \nreinforce the dry and cool northerly flow at times. \n\nWith the northerly flow, the temperatures not flux as they have \nin the past week. They will remain near or slightly below normal. \nLows will generally be in the 40s. Highs will be in the upper 60s to \nlower 70s. \n\nWith moisture sources cut off, no rain is expected this week.",
